    "title": "IDENTIFIED: Person killed in overnight Fresno collision - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Dom McAndrew ,\n5 hours ago\nFRESNO, Calif. ( KSEE/KGPE ) – The pedestrian who died after being struck by a vehicle last week in Fresno has been named by the Fresno County Coroner’s Office.\nThe person killed was identified on Wednesday as 39-year-old Mitchell Wright.\nOfficers responded early in the morning on June 25 to Blackstone and Olive avenues after a report that a vehicle had hit someone. When officers arrived, they found the 39-year-old in the middle of the roadway. They were taken to a local hospital, where they died.\nInvestigators say the driver was traveling south on Blackstone Avenue toward Olive Avenue when Mitchell Wright, who was crossing outside a crosswalk, was struck.\nThe driver remained at the scene and cooperated with investigators, police said.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS47 and KSEE24 | News from YourCentralValley.com.\n2",
    "summary": "The person killed was identified on Wednesday as 39-year-old Mitchell Wright. Officers responded early in the morning on June 25 to Blackstone and Olive avenues after a report that a vehicle had hit someone. Investigators say the driver was traveling south on Blackstone Avenue toward Olive Avenue when Mitchell Wright, who was crossing outside a crosswalk, was struck. The driver remained at the scene and cooperated with investigators, police said. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.",
